@@ -44,3 +44,9 @@ The Swift thresholds, skill objectives, encounter openings and recovery periods
 Save local play notes is opt-in and defaults off. At most sixty world observations are retained. Explicit result feedback retains at most thirty choices (Satisfying, Too difficult, Slow ending). Export play notes includes these observations and feedback without player names, external analytics IDs or network delivery. Closing a collection stops its soundtrack preview.
 
 Release validation is recorded in [the engagement release audit](audit/2026-10-29-engagement-release.md): 221 automated tests, a source-only cold build and exact-source local Chromium checks for collection/aiming, recovery, 40 dialog layout states, 38 cinematic caption/action states, controlled drawing comparison, 3600 sustained frames and nineteen sampled flash screens. The browser evidence records its source/fixture identity and scope. Physical phone checks and enjoyment studies remain separate; these checks do not establish native sharing, OS behavior, accessibility conformance or measured player engagement. Deployment/readback and existing-client update evidence are recorded separately in the same audit.
+
+## Reward ceremonies and mastery entry
+
+Selecting a world from Mastery & rewards starts official Practice with a mastery intent flag; it does not change scoring or medal requirements. Retries preserve that intent. Newly earned medals get a dedicated Three.js/HTML reveal with mastery victory music, separate from the score summary. First completion of a world's four-medal set gets the World mastered crest; the 64th medal gets the Prism Master crown finale. Already-owned medals are never announced as newly earned. Ordinary Adventure/Daily/official Practice awards are recognized before the normal world story; mastery-entry rewards lead directly to medal-focused results and the collection.
+
+The authored page owns the medal SVG symbols, reusable token template and semantic ceremony. CSS styles earned/locked/new states; the renderer decorates them with a reusable, bounded scene. Reduced motion reveals all awards immediately in a stationary composition; mute and volume preferences apply, and continuation is always explicit. Failed progress writes expose a save retry and recovery guidance instead of claiming the awards were saved. The cabinet retains an all-64 completion presentation after the ceremony, including for imported collections.
